{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_05dde6133be9fd587d66671183a2404cfec7e440b612a5d1c8769983ecd10b03"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"AGENTS.md instructions are loaded from a global path (`~/.openinterpreter/AGENTS.md`) and project files from repo root to the current directory, with closer files taking precedence and a `project_doc_max_bytes` cap."}],"claim_ids":["clm_05dde6133be9fd587d66671183a2404cfec7e440b612a5d1c8769983ecd10b03"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_2f1e21cfadf247d3be317b78ea325fec","id":"pg_288a35291d0d5a3b98252eb8780b9d15","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/openinterpreter-openinterpreter-docs-agents-md-md-860153a5318d-2eb8780b9d15.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_9385e58e3393561eb2a0d5b44c8aabc4"],"title":"openinterpreter/openinterpreter/docs/agents_md.md @ 860153a5318d","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_2f1e21cfadf247d3be317b78ea325fec"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_e70cd037b6c851d649093a7e66fe0506d004c0e28859cf8e1c301c9fd2265797"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Permission profiles offer finer-grained filesystem and network rules than sandbox_mode, including workspace roots, deny globs for secret files, per-domain network allow/deny, and Unix socket exceptions; network starts disabled."}],"claim_ids":["clm_e70cd037b6c851d649093a7e66fe0506d004c0e28859cf8e1c301c9fd2265797"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_2f1e21cfadf247d3be317b78ea325fec","id":"pg_48872b2387bb56bea6a353ad8e70c7ae","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/openinterpreter-openinterpreter-docs-permissions-md-860153a5318d-53ad8e70c7ae.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_12bc48f45af55590971cac53e951d92d"],"title":"openinterpreter/openinterpreter/docs/permissions.md @ 860153a5318d","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_2f1e21cfadf247d3be317b78ea325fec"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_7e403e331726693a0b7735f24a9cc8b48413a32c41d5d46af13b4e5e6b23409f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Sandbox modes (read-only, workspace-write, danger-full-access) and approval policies (untrusted, on-request, never) are separate controls; OS enforcement uses Seatbelt on macOS and Bubblewrap/seccomp on Linux/WSL, failing closed when a policy cannot be enforced."}],"claim_ids":["clm_7e403e331726693a0b7735f24a9cc8b48413a32c41d5d46af13b4e5e6b23409f"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_2f1e21cfadf247d3be317b78ea325fec","id":"pg_d7d08fa898db50d9b1407a25f4e9d062","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/openinterpreter-openinterpreter-docs-sandbox-md-860153a5318d-7a25f4e9d062.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_be833f0475b25e7d98275929ebc94903"],"title":"openinterpreter/openinterpreter/docs/sandbox.md @ 860153a5318d","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_2f1e21cfadf247d3be317b78ea325fec"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_06a47d8b815a11a11d63da1f0fda96959422e1493a01fef878f0593124a05f8d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Custom OpenAI-compatible providers can be defined under `[model_providers.<id>]` with base_url, env_key, and wire_api (responses or chat), and credentials should come from environment variables or a credential store."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1044290e3e54ffa96294ef734e6292c9db6720574e2542bf2b07d5be7f26ee19"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"MCP servers are configured under `[mcp_servers]` supporting stdio commands and streamable HTTP servers via `url`, with per-server default tool approval modes."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ece22aadb879f8f6abcc37cab2e3011a63cfdaefd538b85ce0ab5b993ac69bdc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Configuration is read from TOML files at user level (`~/.openinterpreter/config.toml`) and trusted project level (`.openinterpreter/config.toml`), with CLI `-c` overrides applying per invocation."}],"claim_ids":["clm_06a47d8b815a11a11d63da1f0fda96959422e1493a01fef878f0593124a05f8d","clm_1044290e3e54ffa96294ef734e6292c9db6720574e2542bf2b07d5be7f26ee19","clm_ece22aadb879f8f6abcc37cab2e3011a63cfdaefd538b85ce0ab5b993ac69bdc"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_2f1e21cfadf247d3be317b78ea325fec","id":"pg_d917194e7d1d53008ee3dcd8e9d12348","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/openinterpreter-openinterpreter-docs-config-md-860153a5318d-dcd8e9d12348.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_4971cfbe1898572aadd09b2cbc430a69"],"title":"openinterpreter/openinterpreter/docs/config.md @ 860153a5318d","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_2f1e21cfadf247d3be317b78ea325fec"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_01b6ccd6ecf6c879cab94da94e4746db6ba95e6da55b89ada882dbce83cc8c4b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Installation is via a shell script on macOS/Linux and a PowerShell script on Windows; a session starts by typing `i` or `interpreter` in the terminal."},{"claim_ids":["clm_09ac983a39b4d65f13385126ea847a3ed2410dd8a2f86da2e62339d6adfb81d1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product runs as an Agent Client Protocol agent via `interpreter acp` and speaks the Codex exec protocol, allowing a one-line Codex SDK binary override to `interpreter`."},{"claim_ids":["clm_239abd2d6b9914731550e176c18fb836cb84912c972f099379828ef1a7bb66ce"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Portability is a stated product goal: shared AGENTS.md, `.agents/skills` directories, MCP, ACP, and the Codex exec protocol are preferred, with `~/.openinterpreter` reserved for config and runtime state lacking shared standards."},{"claim_ids":["clm_502e0bfc07f58f526d8ac2b2cba4799bb0ecc9cba616da1ea02a97b05b7fceae"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project describes itself as a fork of OpenAI's Codex focused on emulating the agent harness that gets the best performance from low-cost models."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7e8143552cce71c9bb0c6de3217ca379f828d8b4cb6a83c00de7e16fb27e8c66"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: provider and model membership is generated rather than maintained as Rust lists, refreshed from `codex-rs` with `python3 scripts/write_provider_catalog.py`, and a `scripts/test-codex-sdk-compat.sh` script provides a local provider-free compatibility check."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9333519fc8b24b9e49e862e0364b9dad2f6b7221cace53cbffbd8f4db9c96b3f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README notes this is the new Rust version of Open Interpreter; the original Python project continues as a community-maintained fork elsewhere."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d7b9486e6cfb860a0f62c3d700c971b7ec5e17eacb747a04c55a7a45fc91422a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product ships a QA skill that can drive web apps in a real browser via agent-browser or operate native apps via trycua."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ed6d237a89577ba47c72a9369f169b5442a03bae9762ab3cfabe0596bd01de42"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Skills live in shared `.agents/skills` or `~/.agents/skills` directories; legacy product-specific skill directories remain readable for compatibility."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f66d2049e19841f61aa7cd559f21a9b6523a74bacd502f945f740efe37036cef"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A `/harness` TUI command switches the active harness among listed modes including native, claude-code, kimi-code, qwen-code, deepseek-tui, swe-agent, and minimal."}],"claim_ids":["clm_01b6ccd6ecf6c879cab94da94e4746db6ba95e6da55b89ada882dbce83cc8c4b","clm_09ac983a39b4d65f13385126ea847a3ed2410dd8a2f86da2e62339d6adfb81d1","clm_239abd2d6b9914731550e176c18fb836cb84912c972f099379828ef1a7bb66ce","clm_502e0bfc07f58f526d8ac2b2cba4799bb0ecc9cba616da1ea02a97b05b7fceae","clm_7e8143552cce71c9bb0c6de3217ca379f828d8b4cb6a83c00de7e16fb27e8c66","clm_9333519fc8b24b9e49e862e0364b9dad2f6b7221cace53cbffbd8f4db9c96b3f","clm_d7b9486e6cfb860a0f62c3d700c971b7ec5e17eacb747a04c55a7a45fc91422a","clm_ed6d237a89577ba47c72a9369f169b5442a03bae9762ab3cfabe0596bd01de42","clm_f66d2049e19841f61aa7cd559f21a9b6523a74bacd502f945f740efe37036cef"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_2f1e21cfadf247d3be317b78ea325fec","id":"pg_fb1c5bd71d6754cfabdb76eb3eeee196","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/openinterpreter-openinterpreter-readme-md-860153a5318d-76eb3eeee196.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_d3339742ebab53fb96c8c109c736cfee"],"title":"openinterpreter/openinterpreter/README.md @ 860153a5318d","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_2f1e21cfadf247d3be317b78ea325fec"}
